WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:06.450
there's the very interesting shift in the
second choices of voters for the 2020 democratic

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.450
erratic

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:12.370
presidential candidates that now is starting
to increase the calls for Elizabeth Warren

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:17.519
to drop out in order to help Bernie Sanders
overtake Joe Biden.

00:00:17.519 --> 00:00:19.230
And I want to talk about this with you.

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:20.609
This is a conversation.

00:00:20.609 --> 00:00:25.720
I'm just the Messenger here of the data and
then I will analyze the data to the best of

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:26.890
my ability.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:30.220
I want to be clear and I know people always
write to me, they say, David, you don't have

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:31.869
to do these dumb disclaimers.

00:00:31.869 --> 00:00:33.230
Trust me, I do.

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:36.090
I am not calling for anyone to drop out.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:42.010
I am not saying it's Warren who should drop
instead of Bernie because she's a woman either

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:43.680
consciously or unconsciously.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:47.470
I'm just telling you, this is something we've
been talking about for a while.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:52.870
It's complex, it's multifaceted and I want
to give you the data as it is and then I will

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:55.110
react to it and then we can have a conversation.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:57.560
So let me set it up for you right now.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:04.119
According to most national polls, I think
all really, um, Joe Biden is in first place

00:01:04.119 --> 00:01:08.240
in the 2020 democratic primary with Bernie
Sanders.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:12.399
Second place in most polls, Elizabeth Warren,
third in most polls, there are some polls

00:01:12.399 --> 00:01:17.009
were Bernie and Warren are statistically tied
some in which Elizabeth Warren is ahead by

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:18.150
a sometimes a point or so.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:25.249
So if you look at the numbers, you see that
if you add Bernie's polling to Elizabeth Warren's

00:01:25.249 --> 00:01:30.000
polling, you get a number that is bigger than
Joe Biden's in this case, if we look at the

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.319
morning consult poll from September 2nd to
eighth, you see that Bernie and Warren together

00:01:35.319 --> 00:01:39.060
have 37% to Joe Biden's 33.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:40.060
Okay.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:44.380
So the idea that keeps coming up and that's
being discussed and that people contact me

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:50.520
about is listen, Bernie and Warren are the
two strong progressive candidates.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:53.880
Aren't they taking votes away from each other?

00:01:53.880 --> 00:02:00.259
Bernie drops out, his support goes to Warren
Warren over, uh, overtakes Joe Biden or, uh,

00:02:00.259 --> 00:02:04.270
conversely, if it was with Warren, drops out,
her support goes to Bernie Sanders.

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:06.210
He overtakes Joe Biden.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:07.210
Progressive's win.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:08.210
Okay.

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:12.550
Now up until now, I've been saying the data
doesn't seem to confirm that because in the

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:15.200
polls I have been looking at the top.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:21.380
Second choice for Bernie voters has been Biden
and the top second choice for Warren voters

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:26.380
has been Kamala Harris, which might seem surprising
because ideologically it doesn't make sense,

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:32.080
but along demographic lines it does make more
sense, but people have started sending me

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:38.110
recent data from once again this morning consult
poll conducted up until two days ago ending

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:41.560
on September 8th saying, David, the numbers
have changed.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:46.140
Warren voters now are saying Bernie is their
top second choice.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:51.170
It would put Bernie into the lead if Elizabeth
Warren were to drop out.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:53.130
But is this actually what the data says?

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:54.130
Yes and no.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:55.340
Let's actually look at it.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:03:01.310
It is indeed true that in the most recent
morning consult poll, the top second choice

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:08.260
for Bernie voters is Joe Biden and the top
second choice of Warren voters is now Bernie

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.260
Sanders.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:12.780
Elizabeth Warren voters are now saying more
about Bernie than any other candidate that

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.980
elicit if Elizabeth Warren were to drop out
or not be the candidate, they would prefer

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:17.400
Bernie Sanders.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.840
But let's do the math.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:25.510
If Elizabeth Warren were to leave the race,
24% of her support would go to Bernie.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:30.210
21% would go to Joe Biden, and 19% would go
to Carmela Harris.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:36.620
And when you actually look at the numbers,
if you divide up Elizabeth Warren's 16 percentage

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:43.260
points and consider that only slightly more
of her voters would go to Bernie than Biden,

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:45.370
it actually wouldn't put Bernie in the lead.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:50.820
What Elizabeth Warren dropping out would do
on the basis of second choices in this poll,

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:58.750
it would put Biden at 36% and Bernie at 25%
and Kamel Harris at 10% it would not put Bernie

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:00.280
Sanders into the lead.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:04.780
Her percentage points, 16 percentage points
would go disproportionately.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:09.540
A plurality would go to Bernie Sanders, but
some would go to Biden as well, and it wouldn't

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:11.040
be enough to put Bernie in the lead.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:17.470
So does this invalidate the idea that the
progressive movement would have something

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.620
to gain if either Bernie or Warren dropped
out?

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:25.600
Now it's possible that at some point, that
is a conversation that we'll have to be had

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:28.870
if the first few primaries don't sort it out
on its own.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:35.810
I don't think that we need now to start saying
things like top three candidates should bail.

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:40.180
Now, we've been talking about, listen, if
you're not even pulling 1%, if you're not

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:45.560
even pulling 2% six, seven months into this
race, if you're not even making it into the

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:48.940
debates, what is your path to victory?

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:52.800
But I believe that the conversation about
Bernie and Warren dropping out now is premature.

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:58.700
Now, if we get past the Iowa caucus and the
New Hampshire primary and we get into February,

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:02.830
March, I forget exactly what the schedule
is, but I'm sort of estimating here.

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:08.910
Uh, and it does seem as though bearing in
mind the 15% vesting threshold that many primaries

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:14.680
have in all of these other things that Joe
Biden is ultimately going to squeak by because

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:19.090
of the division of the progressive movement
between Bernie Sanders and Elizabeth Warren.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:22.710
And the second choice data starts to suggest
that one or the other would take the lead

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:23.710
over Biden.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:27.740
If the other word to drop out, then we actually
will have something to talk about.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:32.770
I think there is a very good chance that support
consolidates between now and the first handful

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:37.560
of primaries and that ultimately the system,
we'll sort this out.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:41.880
And if the progressive movement is the strongest
movement, uh, then it will win out.

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:47.680
But the point is, even this new poll does
not show that there is a clear path to victory

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.100
over Joe Biden.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:51.710
If either Bernie Sanders or Elizabeth Warren
were to drop out.

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:56.570
Now you could still believe that for intangible
reasons, that might be the case for momentum

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:57.570
reasons.

00:05:57.570 --> 00:05:58.570
That might be the case.

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:01.190
But the data don't actually bear that out
right now.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:02.190
Let me know what you think.

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:02.199
I do want to hear from you about this

